          ]
        }
      ],
      "limits": "Malformed/publicly assembled element boundary; generated canonical elements under valid small field assumptions avoid it. Raw FiniteField::new already documents a separate irreducibility trust premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "RFA-F004",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Binary operations disagree on out-of-carrier masks and raw phases",
      "statement": "For valid GF4 modulus7, mul(4,1)=0 but mul(1,4)=3; arbitrary usize arguments are neither refused nor consistently reduced. Public BinaryPauli.phase allows values>3; adjoint uses 4-phase and mul adds raw u8 values, yielding debug overflow/panic or wrapped release arithmetic instead of typed refusal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_number_theory/src/binary_field.rs",
          "sha256": "7549563d8b3af98d07ee7edffa4c80c7c688fb03a343e976fc96763d60ee14b9",
