    {
      "id": "RFA-F009",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Gaussian norm realization needs reduced rational limbs",
      "statement": "realize_norm tests numerator and denominator separately with two_squares without reducing the rational. BigRational::new_raw(3,3) represents1, whose Gaussian norm witness is1+0i, but the numerator3 immediately returns None. In the same module norm_class cancels the two odd3 valuations and propose_obstruction returns none. The negative realization verdict is therefore representation-dependent.",
